From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Add the remaining pin
 bank supplies

Banks PE, PF, PJ and PK of the pin controller and bank PM of the
r-pin controller have no supply in the DT, so the pin controllers use
dummy regulators for them.

In the schematic, banks PE and PK run from BLDO1 (1.8 V in this device
tree; the schematic gives no voltage), which also
feeds VCC-MCSI and has no node yet. Bank PJ runs from VCC33-LCD
(SWOUT1) with no series part. Bank PF switches between VCC-IO (SWOUT2)
and VCC18-PF (CLDO5) through its power-source; it names VCC-IO, the
selection after reset. The VCC-PM ball of bank PM goes through RA13
(0R) to VCC-PL (ALDO1); the net named VCC-PM on CLDO1 does not reach
the SoC.

Add BLDO1 at 1.8 V and always on, as the boot chain leaves it: VCC-MCSI
and the camera signals on J5 have no consumer, so the regulator core
would otherwise switch the rail off. Add the five supplies. Bank PL
stays without a supply, for the reason given at ALDO1.

The A733 pin controllers do not program the withstand voltage from the
supplies, so no register changes.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: with one line of each bank requested, the
five supplies resolve to their regulators instead of the dummy one,
BLDO1 stays on after the regulator late cleanup, and the SoC's bank
voltage detector reads 1.8 V for PE and PK and 3.3 V for PJ and PM.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 36 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 027cdedfab7f..475449dc57c3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -403,8 +403,12 @@ &pio {
 	vcc-pb-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
 	vcc-pc-supply = <&reg_cldo5>;
 	vcc-pd-supply = <&reg_swout1>;
+	vcc-pe-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
+	vcc-pf-supply = <&reg_swout2>;	/* or VCC18-PF, see power-source */
 	vcc-pg-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
 	vcc-ph-supply = <&reg_swout2>;
+	vcc-pj-supply = <&reg_swout1>;
+	vcc-pk-supply = <&reg_bldo1>;
 };
 
 &r_i2c0 {
@@ -434,13 +438,13 @@ axp318: pmic@36 {
 
 		regulators {
 			/*
-			 * VCC-PL: bank PL (the PMIC bus pins), bank PG, the
-			 * EEPROM and the TWI0 pull-ups. Always on: the PMIC bus
-			 * runs on bank PL. Bank PL has no vcc-pl-supply on
+			 * VCC-PL: bank PL (the PMIC bus pins), banks PG and PM,
+			 * the EEPROM and the TWI0 pull-ups. Always on: the PMIC
+			 * bus runs on bank PL. Bank PL has no vcc-pl-supply on
 			 * r_pio: the PMIC sits on r_i2c0 (PL0/PL1), and the pin
 			 * driver requests the bank supply when r_i2c0 gets its
-			 * pins, so the supply of ALDO1 would defer the pins
-			 * and the PMIC that provides ALDO1 would never probe.
+			 * pins, so the supply of ALDO1 would defer the pins and
+			 * the PMIC that provides ALDO1 would never probe.
 			 */
 			reg_aldo1: aldo1 {
 				regulator-name = "vcc-pl";
@@ -456,7 +460,7 @@ reg_dcdc1: dcdc1 {
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
-			/* 1.8 V I/O: eMMC VCCQ, bank PC */
+			/* 1.8 V I/O: eMMC VCCQ, bank PC, VCC18-PF of bank PF */
 			reg_cldo5: cldo5 {
 				regulator-name = "vcc-pc";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
@@ -466,8 +470,8 @@ reg_cldo5: cldo5 {
 
 			/*
 			 * Ethernet PHY, bank PD through R251, bank PJ, the
-			 * TWI2/TWI7 pull-ups on J11. Always on: bank PJ and the
-			 * pull-ups name no supply.
+			 * TWI2/TWI7 pull-ups on J11. Always on: the pull-ups
+			 * name no supply.
 			 */
 			reg_swout1: swout1 {
 				regulator-name = "vcc33-lcd";
@@ -483,6 +487,17 @@ reg_swout2: swout2 {
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
 
+			/*
+			 * 1.8 V I/O: banks PE and PK, VCC-MCSI and the camera
+			 * signals on J5. Always on: VCC-MCSI names no supply.
+			 */
+			reg_bldo1: bldo1 {
+				regulator-name = "vcc-pe-pk-mcsi";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
 			reg_dcdc3: dcdc3 {
 				regulator-name = "vdd-cpub";
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
@@ -575,6 +590,11 @@ usbc_sbu: endpoint {
 	};
 };
 
+&r_pio {
+	/* No vcc-pl-supply: see ALDO1 */
+	vcc-pm-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+};
+
 &rtc {
 	clocks = <&r_ccu CLK_BUS_R_RTC>, <&osc>,
 		 <&r_ccu CLK_R_AHB>, <&ext_osc32k>;
